            <div xml:id="d1586">

                <pb facs="1005" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg889"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/75.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Imperial German Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 16, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: The Imperial Government
                    has heard from Mexico that the Constitutionalist Government has appropriated <pb
                        facs="1006" n="890" xml:id="pg890"/> to itself the warehouse of the German
                    firm of Eversbusch with goods worth 100,000 pesos at Tampico. The Imperial
                    Consulate at Tampico has received no reply to his protest to the said
                    Government. Furthermore, German subjects and commercial houses are still opposed
                    to having contributions levied upon them.</p>
                <p>I am therefore instructed most respectfully to ask your excellency that the
                    Government of the United States will bring its influence to bear on the
                    Constitutionalist Government in Mexico for the protection of German subjects and
                    firms from injustice and imposition and for the release of their property.</p>
                <p>Looking forward to your excellency’s obliging answer,</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Imperial Ambassador: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kurt von Lersner</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
